	<item>
		<title>GPT-6 Astra sees the matrix and reprograms other AI models directly through their weights</title>
		<link>https://the-decoder.com/gpt-6-astra-sees-the-matrix-and-reprograms-other-ai-models-directly-through-their-weights/</link>
					<comments>https://the-decoder.com/gpt-6-astra-sees-the-matrix-and-reprograms-other-ai-models-directly-through-their-weights/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Maximilian Schreiner]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 15:44:44 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AI research]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Artificial Intelligence]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AI training]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://the-decoder.com/?p=42387</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p><img width="1376" height="768" src="https://the-decoder.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Weight-Space-Programming.png" class="attachment-full size-full wp-post-image" alt="" style="height: auto; margin-bottom: 10px;" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high" /></p>
<p>        MIT researchers show that OpenAI's GPT-6 Astra can read and deliberately rewrite the weights of other AI models without traditional training. In one experiment, Astra boosted a Qwen model's math accuracy from 7.9 to 48.1 percent by changing just 0.016 percent of its weights. The approach could fundamentally simplify AI optimization but still hits clear limits.</p>
<p>The article <a href="https://the-decoder.com/gpt-6-astra-sees-the-matrix-and-reprograms-other-ai-models-directly-through-their-weights/">GPT-6 Astra sees the matrix and reprograms other AI models directly through their weights</a> appeared first on <a href="https://the-decoder.com">The Decoder</a>.</p>
]]></description>
		
					<wfw:commentRss>https://the-decoder.com/gpt-6-astra-sees-the-matrix-and-reprograms-other-ai-models-directly-through-their-weights/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
