		<item>
		<title>Exit polls show AI ranked last among voter priorities in the 2026 U.S. midterms</title>
		<link>https://the-decoder.com/exit-polls-show-ai-ranked-last-among-voter-priorities-in-the-2026-u-s-midterms/</link>
					<comments>https://the-decoder.com/exit-polls-show-ai-ranked-last-among-voter-priorities-in-the-2026-u-s-midterms/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Matthias Bastian]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 10:45:54 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AI in practice]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Artificial Intelligence]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Short News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[USA]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://the-decoder.com/?p=42380</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p><img width="1456" height="816" src="https://the-decoder.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/usa_flag_data_stream.png" class="attachment-full size-full wp-post-image" alt="illustration of the US flag in an abstract data stream" style="height: auto; margin-bottom: 10px;" decoding="async" /></p>
<p>        In the 2026 U.S. midterm elections, AI ranked last among campaign issues: only 56 percent of respondents cited AI and data centers as an important factor. According to NBC exit polls, corruption (90 percent) and the cost of living (89 percent) clearly dominated, despite growing public attention to the issue.</p>
<p>The article <a href="https://the-decoder.com/exit-polls-show-ai-ranked-last-among-voter-priorities-in-the-2026-u-s-midterms/">Exit polls show AI ranked last among voter priorities in the 2026 U.S. midterms</a> appeared first on <a href="https://the-decoder.com">The Decoder</a>.</p>
]]></description>
		
