		<category><![CDATA[OpenAI]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://the-decoder.com/?p=42368</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p><img width="1752" height="989" src="https://the-decoder.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/openai_ai_hardware.png" class="attachment-full size-full wp-post-image" alt="" style="height: auto; margin-bottom: 10px;" decoding="async" /></p>
<p>        OpenAI's hardware team used GPT-6 Astra to design a device for the Codex coding agent in under a week, handling everything from the enclosure to the circuit board to the firmware. Several revision rounds were needed before production because the model didn't always account for manufacturing tolerances. A newer internal model scores significantly higher on OpenAI's engineering benchmark, though the company isn't sharing details.</p>
<p>The article <a href="https://the-decoder.com/openai-says-gpt-6-astra-designed-a-hardware-device-from-scratch-in-under-a-week/">OpenAI says GPT-6 Astra designed a hardware device from scratch in under a week</a> appeared first on <a href="https://the-decoder.com">The Decoder</a>.</p>
]]></description>
		
